      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Getting Started with CloudScale API\n\n## Authentication\nTo access the CloudScale API, you must first create an API key in your dashboard settings. Once generated, paste the key into the `X-Auth-Key` header of every request or use the provided environment variable `CLOUDSCALE_API_KEY` for seamless integration.\n\n## Sending Your First Request\nBegin by calling the `/v1/db/signup` endpoint to create a new database schema. The body should contain essential configuration details like region preference and memory allocation. For example, pass a JSON object with `\"region\": \"us-east-1\"` and `\"memory\": \"2gb\"`.\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.cloudscale.io/v1/db/signup \\\n  -H \"X-Auth-Key: YOUR_API_KEY_HERE\" \\\n  -d '{\"region\": \"us-east-1\", \"memory\": \"2gb\"}'\n```\n\n## Verifying Success\nUpon receiving a `200 OK` response with a unique database ID, your database is ready for immediate use. You can now proceed to define models or execute queries against this new instance directly within the CloudScale console or via further API calls.",
