      "content": "# Getting Started with CloudScale API\n\n## 1. Authentication and Setup\n### Creating Your API Key\nTo access the CloudScale API, you must first generate a unique API key from the user dashboard. Navigate to the \"Developer Tools\" tab and select \"Generate Key\" from the sidebar menu. \n\n### Using the Key Effectively\nOnce you have your key, there are two primary methods for authentication:\n*   **Header Method:** Manually paste the key into the custom header field named `X-Auth-Key` on every request.\n*   **Environment Variable:** Set the `CLOUDSCALE_API_KEY` variable in your local `.env` file for seamless, secure integration without repetitive headers.\n*   **Best Practices:** We recommend using the environment variable for production deployments to avoid exposing secrets in HTTP logs or endpoint headers.\n\n## 2. Multiple Endpoint Practices\n### The Signup Endpoint\nTo initialize your infrastructure, call the `/v1/db/signup` endpoint. This is the entry point for creating your first managed database schema.\n*   Ensure the method is set to POST.\n*   The URL must include the version suffix `/v1`.\n*   Never replace `YOUR_API_KEY` in real",
